invariant: INV-14
file: tls.c
catches: webpki_session_host
reason: the webpki client of a host object stops asking for the caller's
  description of its CPU, so ch_connect sends a ClientHello for a
  configuration that never set ch_cfg.cpu. test/webpki_session_cpu.h
  requires CH_EINVAL before a byte leaves for 0.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    // The caller's description of its CPU (cpu_cfg.h), before
    // webpki_cfg_ok's suite rule reads it.
    if (!cpu_bits_ok(cfg)) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
--- new
